  #line-at(70.08pt, 257.04pt, "ABSTRACT")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.48pt, 257.04pt, "Quantum transduction, which enables the coherent conversion of quantum information between ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 268.56pt, "disparate physical platforms, is a cornerstone for realizing scalable and interoperable quantum networks. Among ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 279.72pt, "various approaches, parametric frequency mixing processes such as four-wave mixing (FWM) offer a promising ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 291pt, "pathway toward efficient and low-noise transduction. In this work, we demonstrate the feasibility of coherent quantum ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 302.16pt, "state transfer by indirectly verifying high-fidelity wavefunction’s phase mapping (>99%) from the input field to the ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 313.44pt, "generated output field wave. Using a gas-filled hollow-core capillary fiber, we systematically investigate spectral ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 324.48pt, "phase evolution across a broad range, including infrared (IR) to ultraviolet (UV) transitions, as well as conversions ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 335.76pt, "from telecom-band (1550 nm) to visible (516 nm) and deep-UV (308 nm) wavelengths. Our results reveal that strong ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 346.92pt, "phase coherence can be maintained throughout these diverse conversion regimes. Because quantum properties such ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 358.08pt, "as coherence and entanglement are intrinsically encoded in both the amplitude and phase of a photonic wavefunction, ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 369.36pt, "preserving spectral phase is essential for faithful quantum information transfer. We further show that efficient and ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 380.52pt, "phase-preserving transduction can be achieved by tuning system parameters, offering valuable insights into nonlinear ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 391.68pt, "coupling dynamics. These findings establish a promising foundation for advancing FWM-based quantum transduction ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 402.84pt, "schemes and open new avenues for integrating heterogeneous quantum systems across wide spectral domains within ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 414.12pt, "future quantum communication networks. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.08pt, 436.92pt, "Keywords:")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(115.56pt, 436.92pt, " Quantum transduction, photon frequency mixing, spectral phase mapping, gas-filled hollow-core capillary ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 448.2pt, "fiber ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.746pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.08pt, 477.24pt, "1.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(87.6pt, 477.24pt, "Introduction")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.08pt, 488.52pt, "The rapid advancement of quantum technologies hinges on the ability to efficiently interface and interconnect a wide ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 501.36pt, "variety of quantum systems [1,2]. Quantum transduction plays a pivotal role in enabling future quantum architectures ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 514.2pt, "by bridging disparate physical platforms [3,4], thereby supporting distributed quantum computing [5,6], hybrid ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 527.04pt, "quantum devices[7], and advanced quantum sensing[8]. A wide range of quantum transduction methods has been ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 540pt, "developed to meet the demands of quantum networking[4], where transducers serve as critical interfaces between ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 552.84pt, "quantum processors and optical communication channels. For example, the conversion of quantum information ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 565.68pt, "between microwave and optical domains[9–13], is essential for linking superconducting quantum processors with ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 578.52pt, "long-distance optical communication channels. Conventional approaches, such as piezo-optomechanical and ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 591.36pt, "electromechanical transducers, utilize mechanical modes as intermediaries to facilitate this conversion. While recent ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 604.32pt, "experiments[10] have demonstrated conversion efficiencies on the order of (0.88 ± 0.16) × 10⁻⁵ with signal-to-noise ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 617.16pt, "ratios (SNR) exceeding unity, theoretical models suggest the potential for much higher efficiencies, exceeding 50%, ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 630pt, "and in some cases approaching near-unity levels, especially when employing impedance-matched designs or advanced ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 642.84pt, "materials such as antiferromagnetic topological insulators. Despite ongoing challenges, including mechanical noise, ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 655.68pt, "cavity losses, and the stringent requirement to preserve quantum coherence, recent progress underscores the central ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 668.76pt, "importance of transduction technologies in integrating heterogeneous quantum platforms within future ")
  #line-at(70.08pt, 681.6pt, "architectures[7,14,15]. ")
]

