]

// arXiv source page 12
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-12.png", width: 434.5pt), 80.5pt, 111pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.745pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.723pt, 767.513pt, "12 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.759pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.199pt, 511.796pt, "Figure 7 Spectral phase mapping correlations under (a-b) signal 1550 nm, intermediary 515 nm and idler field 303nm and (c-d)  ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 523.312pt, "signal 1550 nm, intermediary 775 nm and idler field 516 nm: between the output idler field and output signal pulses, and between ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 534.956pt, "the output idler field and input signal pulse, as a function of varying input intermediary energy and the bandwidth.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.694pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.199pt, 558.959pt, "It is also noteworthy that, in this case, the intermediary bandwidth is limited to the range of 1.5–4.5 nm, in contrast to ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 571.916pt, "the broader range explored in the previous cases. As shown in Figure 6d–e and Figure 7, the correlation coefficients ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 584.755pt, "drop rapidly when the intermediary bandwidth exceeds approximately 2 nm. This behavior arises because, in the case ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 597.594pt, "of positive quadratic modulation, the output field initially acquires an inverted (negative quadratic) phase structure ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 610.436pt, "relative to the input field. However, as the input intermediary energy increases, nonlinear effects such as SPM and ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 623.272pt, "XPM in the output field channel become increasingly significant. This is also related to the intermediary's ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 636.239pt, "monochromatic characteristic. These nonlinear interactions lead to the spectral broadening of the output field pulse, ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 649.075pt, "which inherently reshapes its phase profile toward a positive quadratic form. Consequently, the output spectral phase ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 662.035pt, "assumes a parabolic shape, and the corresponding pulse duration shortens due to the combined influence of nonlinear ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 674.877pt, "phase accumulation and group velocity dispersion. This phenomenon is less prominent in the previous negative-")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 687.716pt, "quadratic case, where either the phase modulation formats were matched or the nonlinear effects were less disruptive. ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 700.676pt, "In the positive quadratic modulation scenario, this interplay/compensation between nonlinear broadening and phase ")
  #line-at(70.199pt, 713.512pt, "inversion becomes a dominant factor limiting the fidelity of phase transfer. ")
]

